1e:["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","code",null,{"children":"supported_platform_properties"}]," is the matching contract between this scheduler\nand its workers. Each value is a match rule (",["$","code",null,{"children":"exact"}],", ",["$","code",null,{"children":"minimum"}],", ",["$","code",null,{"children":"priority"}],", or\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"ignore"}],"). A worker that advertises a property the scheduler does not list is\nrejected at registration (",["$","code",null,{"children":"Unknown platform property"}],"), and an action that\nrequests one is rejected the same way. Getting this out of sync with the\nworkers is the single most common reason actions sit in the queue forever; see\n",["$","$L77",null,{"href":"/remote-execution/platform-properties","children":"platform properties"}]," for how the two\nhalves line up."]}]
