29:["$","div",null,{"className":"my-6 flex gap-3 rounded-xl border px-5 py-4 border-amber-500/40 bg-amber-50/60 text-foreground dark:bg-amber-500/10","role":"alert","children":[["$","svg",null,{"width":"20","height":"20","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"1.75","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"mt-0.5 shrink-0 text-amber-600 dark:text-amber-400","aria-hidden":"true","children":"$18:props:children:0:props:children"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex-1 [&>p]:my-0 [&>p+p]:mt-2","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-1 font-mono text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em]","children":"The worker API is a remote code execution endpoint"}],["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","code",null,{"children":"worker_api"}]," is how a process claims to be a worker and receives commands to\nrun. It is on its own listener specifically so that it can be on its own\nnetwork policy. Anything that can reach ",["$","code",null,{"children":":50061"}]," can register as a worker,\nreceive your actions, and return whatever outputs it likes, which then land in\nyour Action Cache and get served to everyone. Keep it inside the cluster.\n",["$","$L77",null,{"href":"/operate/security-hardening#the-worker-api-has-no-authentication","children":"Security hardening"}],"\ncovers the full consequence and what to do about it."]}]]}]]}]
