3a:["$","$Ldf",null,{"type":"multiple","children":[["$","$Le0",null,{"title":"What happens to in-flight actions when a scheduler restarts?","id":"what-happens-to-in-flight-actions-when-a-scheduler-restarts","children":["$","p",null,{"children":"They are lost from the scheduler's point of view. The default scheduler holds\nits queue in process memory and nothing reconstructs it on startup. Clients\nre-submit, so no build fails, but work in progress is repeated. Restart\nschedulers when the queue is shallow."}]}],["$","$Le0",null,{"title":"How do I route GPU or other special-hardware actions?","id":"how-do-i-route-gpu-or-other-special-hardware-actions","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["Advertise the property on the workers that have the hardware\n(",["$","code",null,{"children":"gpu: { values: [\"nvidia-a100\"] }"}],") and declare it as ",["$","code",null,{"children":"\"exact\""}]," in the\nscheduler's ",["$","code",null,{"children":"supported_platform_properties"}],". An action requesting that value\nis then only ever dispatched to a matching worker. Both halves are required:\na worker advertising a property the scheduler does not list is rejected at\nregistration."]}]}],["$","$Le0",null,{"title":"Does fast_slow guarantee everything reaches the slow tier?","id":"does-fast-slow-guarantee-everything-reaches-the-slow-tier","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["No. It never verifies that an object in ",["$","code",null,{"children":"fast"}]," also exists in ",["$","code",null,{"children":"slow"}],". For\nartifacts that must survive a fast-tier wipe (remote execution outputs\nespecially), make sure the write path covers both tiers deliberately. More\nstore gotchas:\n",["$","$L77",null,{"href":"/reference/forge-config/store-overview#faq","children":"Store overview"}],"."]}]}],["$","$Le0",null,{"title":"Can I run this as one process instead of three?","id":"can-i-run-this-as-one-process-instead-of-three","children":["$","p",null,{"children":"Yes, and for a single-machine deployment you should: put the stores,\nschedulers, workers, and servers in one file and run one binary. The split\nexists so the three roles can be scaled and firewalled independently. If you\nhave one machine, you have neither problem."}]}]]}]
