d2:["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","code",null,{"children":"use_namespaces"}]," puts each action in its own process namespace;\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"use_mount_namespace"}]," additionally isolates the worker root in a new mount\nnamespace and gives each action a private ",["$","code",null,{"children":"/tmp"}]," (its own temporary directory,\nbound over ",["$","code",null,{"children":"/tmp"}]," and removed with the action), and only works when\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"use_namespaces"}]," is on. Both are off by default and both are recommended in\nproduction. Set ",["$","code",null,{"children":"isolate_tmp: false"}]," if actions must see the host's ",["$","code",null,{"children":"/tmp"}],",\nfor example because a tool they run lives there. The container\nrunning the worker needs the privileges to create namespaces; the reference\nCompose stack marks the executor service ",["$","code",null,{"children":"privileged: true"}]," for exactly this."]}]
