d5:["$","p",null,{"children":["Setting ",["$","code",null,{"children":"client_ca_file"}]," makes the listener require a client certificate signed by\nthat CA, and ",["$","code",null,{"children":"client_crl_file"}]," lets you revoke one. That is the whole\nauthorization model on the listener: ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"any client with a valid, unrevoked\ncertificate gets full access to that listener's services."}]," No per-identity\nallow-list exists and no mapping from certificate subject to permissions. If you need\nfiner-grained access than \"trusted or not,\" put a proxy in front."]}]
